# Vocabulary versions covered by conformance fixtures in this repo.
# Compare against spec/VOCAB_VERSIONS to detect drift.
# Run scripts/check-downstream-versions.sh from spec/ to check all repos at once.
# Update this file when adding new fixture categories for a vocabulary version.
#
# WHAT A ROW HERE CLAIMS (tightened 2026-08-03, when the fixtures were executed
# by automation for the first time and several rows turned out to be unbacked):
# a version row means at least one fixture instantiates a class that a shape in
# that vocabulary targets, and `scripts/run_conformance.py` evaluates a non-zero
# number of constraints against it. It is a claim of exercised coverage, not of
# mere compatibility, and it is checkable by running the suite. Where a version
# introduced something no fixture reaches, the gap is named rather than implied.
#
# The shapes the suite actually runs against come from the revision named in
# scripts/SPEC_PIN, not from this file. If the two disagree, SPEC_PIN wins and
# the rows below describe a vocabulary CI is not executing, so keep them in step:
# SPEC_PIN's `vocab=` line must repeat the versions below verbatim. As of
# 2026-08-10 both read core=3.5 health=2.6 clinical=1.14 coverage=1.4
# checkup=3.3 pots=1.4, and the pin is the spec PR #17 merge commit d162f68
# (tag vocab/core-v3.5).
#
# 2026-08-08 batch: health 2.6 / clinical 1.14 / coverage 1.4 / checkup 3.3.
# Shapes-only alignment to ratified standards (spec PR the-cascade-protocol/spec#16).
# Five fixtures added, and one KNOWN_FAILURES entry removed rather than re-explained:
#   lab-008  interpretation "I", a HL7 v3 ObservationInterpretation susceptibility
#            code with no member of the five-word enum health v2.5 accepted.
#   lab-009  two labCategory values, two testCode values, interpretation "unknown"
#            (data-absent-reason), and a date-precision performedDate.
#   lab-010  NEGATIVE. Free text is still rejected: the enum was widened to a
#            ratified code system, not deleted.
#   encounter-002  exercises the new clinical:EncounterShape, with a
#            date-precision period and a v3-ActCode encounterClass abbreviation.
#   encounter-003  NEGATIVE. The counterpart clinical:Encounter never had.
# encounter-001 was a KNOWN_FAILURES entry with reason UNSHAPED: it reported
# conforming while evaluating ZERO constraints, because clinical:Encounter had no
# shape. It now evaluates 29, so the entry is gone.
core=3.5
# core=3.5: the ORIGIN axis. cascade:sourceIdentity, a canonical
#   transport-independent organization identity, scheme-prefixed org: / ns: /
#   transport:; cascade:SourceIdentityShape constrains its value wherever it
#   appears and never requires its presence. Fixtures: core/source-identity-org,
#   -namespace and -transport (one per scheme), -two-transports-one-system (the
#   invariant: two transports of one system, differing LABEL and INGESTION,
#   identical ORIGIN), -unprefixed.INVALID (sh:pattern) and -repeated.INVALID
#   (sh:maxCount). Both negatives were measured RED against core 3.4, where the
#   shape does not exist. See fixtures/core/INVENTORY.md.
#   NOT covered by a negative fixture, deliberately: absence of the property,
#   which is not a finding in v3.5. The other 122 fixtures omit it and pass,
#   which exercises that compatibility claim rather than asserting it.
# core=3.4: cascade:ExportManifest modelled on dcat:Dataset and cascade:RecordSummary
#   on void:Dataset, both now defined and shaped. Fixtures: pod-002 (valid manifest
#   carrying a RecordSummary; ExportManifestShape and RecordSummaryShape both fire),
#   pod-004 (manifest with no cascade:schemaVersion, rejected by
#   ExportManifestShape / cascade:schemaVersion / sh:minCount).
#   NOT covered: cascade:InteractionScenario has a shape and no fixture.
# core=3.3: cascade:AIAsserted provenance leaf (ungrounded general-AI content, subClassOf ConsumerGenerated) + cascade:ProxyAgent caregiver-proxy actor (ProxyAgentShape requires actsForPatient, proxyRelationship, proxyGrantedAt). Fixtures: social-002, proxy-001, proxy-002.
